&lt;p&gt;useMemo caches an expensive calculation, React.memo skips unnecessary component re-renders, useRef stores values without causing re-renders, and custom hooks let you reuse stateful logic across components. Together, they make React apps cleaner and faster when used correctly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Quick Difference
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Main Job&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Causes Re-render?&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;useMemo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cache a calculated value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React.memo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Skip re-render if props do not change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;useRef&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Store mutable value or access DOM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Custom Hook&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reuse stateful logic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Depends on hooks inside it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;useMemo memoizes a value, while React.memo memoizes a component.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


useMemo — Cache Expensive Values
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;useMemo stores the result of a calculation and recalculates it only when its dependencies change. It takes a function and a dependency array.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;totalPrice&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;cartItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cartItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real-Time Use in Your Code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In your useProducts hook, totalPrice is calculated from Redux cart items. Without useMemo, this calculation would run on every render — for example, whenever the user types in the search box.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With useMemo, the total is recalculated only when cartItems changes&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


More Examples From Your Code
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;categories&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;category&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This creates a unique, sorted category list. It is recalculated only when products changes.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filteredProducts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// filter + search + sort logic&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;selectedCategory&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;selectedBrands&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;maxPrice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;priceCap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;sortBy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is the best use of useMemo in your code because filtering and sorting a large product list can be expensive. The result is reused until one of these dependencies changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When To Use useMemo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use it when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The calculation is heavy, such as filtering or sorting thousands of items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The result is used by another useMemo, useEffect, or child component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need a stable reference for arrays or objects passed as props.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do not use it for simple values like count + 1; memoization itself has a small cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React.memo — Avoid Unnecessary Re-renders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
React.memo wraps a component and skips its re-render when its props have not changed.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;memo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;memo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ProductCard rendered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"product-card"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;₹&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleCart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Add to Cart&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ProductCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Real-Time Example
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine your product page has:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A search input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Category filter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Price filter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100 product cards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the user types in search, the parent re-renders. Without React.memo, all 100 product cards may re-render. With React.memo, only cards whose product prop changed will re-render.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Important Warning
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This can break React.memo:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ProductCard product={product} handleCart={handleCart} /&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If handleCart is created fresh on every render, its reference changes every time. Then React.memo thinks props changed and re-renders the card anyway.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fix it with useCallback:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addToCart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showSuccess&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; Added To Cart`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;dispatch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now handleCart keeps the same function reference unless dispatch changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;useRef — Value Without Re-render&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
useRef creates a mutable value that persists across renders but does not trigger a re-render when changed. It is commonly used for DOM access, timer IDs, previous values, and avoiding stale values inside callbacks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DOM Reference Example&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchBar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inputRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;focusSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;inputRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;focus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ref&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;inputRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Search products..."&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;focusSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Focus Search&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Timer Example
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timerRef&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTimer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Running...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stopTimer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearInterval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timerRef&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Changing &lt;strong&gt;timerRef.current&lt;/strong&gt; does not re-render the component. That is exactly why it is useful for storing an interval ID.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


useRef vs useState
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Feature&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useState&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;useRef&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Triggers re-render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Best for&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;UI data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;DOM, timers, IDs, previous values&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Access value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;count&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;ref.current&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Value persists&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use useState when the value should appear in the UI. Use useRef when React does not need to re-render for that value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Hooks — Reuse Logic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A custom hook is a JavaScript function whose name starts with use. It can use built-in hooks such as useState, useEffect, useMemo, and useContext, then return values and functions to components.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your useProducts() is a strong custom hook because it combines:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API fetching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loading and error state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Filters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Search&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sorting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redux cart logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Memoized calculations
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loadProducts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Unable to load products.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;loadProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Why Custom Hooks Are Useful
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without a custom hook, product-fetching logic may be copied into multiple pages. With useProducts(), any component can reuse the same logic:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleCart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;totalPrice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clearFilters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This keeps components focused on UI, while the hook handles business logic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
These tools improve performance by avoiding repeated work:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useMemo avoids recalculating filtering, sorting, totals, and derived lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React.memo avoids re-rendering child components when their props are unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useRef avoids re-renders for values that do not affect UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Custom hooks organize logic, making it easier to apply memoization in one place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In your code, the biggest performance win is filteredProducts. If there are 1,000 products, filtering and sorting on every keystroke would be costly. useMemo ensures that work happens only when products, query, filters, or sortBy change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disadvantages and Mistakes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Disadvantage / Mistake&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;useMemo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Adds complexity and memory usage; unnecessary for cheap calculations. react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;useMemo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Wrong dependencies can return stale values.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React.memo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Does not help if props include new objects, arrays, or functions created during every render. react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React.memo&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Comparing props also takes time; overusing it can make performance worse.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;useRef&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Changing ref.current does not update UI, so do not use it for values displayed on screen. react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Custom hooks&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Poorly designed hooks can become too large and difficult to maintain.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Best Practices
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use useMemo only for genuinely expensive or reference-sensitive calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use React.memo for list items and reusable UI components, especially when the parent re-renders often.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pair React.memo with useCallback for functions passed to child components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use useRef for DOM elements, timers, and values that should not trigger renders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep custom hooks focused: one hook for products, one for cart, one for search — rather than one giant hook for everything.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always include every value used inside useMemo in its dependency array.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simple Rule&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need to cache a computed value? Use useMemo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need to stop a component from re-rendering? Use React.memo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need a value that should not cause a re-render? Use useRef.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need to reuse the same stateful logic in multiple components? Create a custom hook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Refresh any half-built React + Laravel app while logged in and you'll see it: the dashboard renders for a split second — no user name, a broken avatar, maybe a flash of the login page first. Then auth "catches up" and everything snaps into place. That flicker is the auth flash, and the fix is embarrassingly small: don't render anything until you know who the visitor is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where the flash comes from
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My auth state lives in an &lt;code&gt;AuthContext&lt;/code&gt;. On mount, if there's a token in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, it calls &lt;code&gt;GET /auth/me&lt;/code&gt; to turn that stored token from a &lt;em&gt;claim&lt;/em&gt; into a &lt;em&gt;fact&lt;/em&gt;. That call is async. Meanwhile React has already rendered. So there's a window — usually a few hundred milliseconds — where &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; but the visitor is actually authenticated. Any route guard that checks &lt;code&gt;user&lt;/code&gt; synchronously will make the wrong call in that window: either bouncing a real user to &lt;code&gt;/login&lt;/code&gt;, or rendering the dashboard with &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; where the user should be.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The gate: a loading flag, checked first
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The context exposes a &lt;code&gt;loading&lt;/code&gt; flag that starts &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; and only flips to &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; after the &lt;code&gt;/me&lt;/code&gt; call settles — success or failure:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;saas_token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/auth/me&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;saas_token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setLoading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Note the &lt;code&gt;catch&lt;/code&gt;: a dead token doesn't just fail — it gets &lt;em&gt;removed&lt;/em&gt;, so the next page load skips the &lt;code&gt;/me&lt;/code&gt; call entirely and goes straight to logged-out. And every protected route checks &lt;code&gt;loading&lt;/code&gt; before it checks anything else:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ProtectedRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useAuth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center bg-gray-100"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"h-10 w-10 animate-spin rounded-full border-4 border-indigo-200 border-t-indigo-600"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Navigate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/login"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The spinner isn't decoration — it's the third auth state. Logged in, logged out, &lt;em&gt;and don't know yet&lt;/em&gt;. Most auth bugs I've seen come from systems that only model the first two.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The admin variant
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same file holds &lt;code&gt;AdminRoute&lt;/code&gt;, which adds one line of real logic:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;admin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Navigate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A non-admin hitting &lt;code&gt;/users&lt;/code&gt; lands on the dashboard, not on a 403 page — deliberate UX: the route simply doesn't exist for them. (The API still enforces &lt;code&gt;role:admin&lt;/code&gt; server-side through the middleware; the frontend redirect is courtesy, not security. Never confuse the two.)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The route tree composes it plainly:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProtectedRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Layout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ProtectedRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;index&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/users"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;element&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AdminRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Users&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;AdminRoute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Route&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The whole &lt;code&gt;Layout&lt;/code&gt; — sidebar, header, all of it — renders only inside &lt;code&gt;ProtectedRoute&lt;/code&gt;, so an unauthenticated visitor never even sees the app shell. &lt;code&gt;/login&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/register&lt;/code&gt; sit outside the guard, public as they should be.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The rule
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Never render an auth-dependent UI on &lt;code&gt;user == null&lt;/code&gt; meaning "logged out". &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt; means "haven't asked the server yet" until the loading flag says otherwise. One boolean, checked first in every guard, and the flash is gone — on refresh, on deep links, on the back button. It's the cheapest reliability win in the whole frontend.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The auth flow above — Sanctum tokens, the &lt;code&gt;/me&lt;/code&gt; re-verification, the route guards — ships in my &lt;a href="https://kamranofficial.gumroad.com/l/mhekoig" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Laravel + React SaaS Starter Kit&lt;/a&gt; ($19 one-time).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;useContext lets any component read shared data from a Context Provider without passing props through every parent component. It is mainly used to avoid prop drilling — passing the same props through many components that do not need them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Is Context?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Context is React’s built-in way to share data across a component tree. A Provider supplies the value, and any child component can read it using useContext.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Real-World Use Cases
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers commonly use Context for data needed in many places:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Theme: light/dark mode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logged-in user: username, role, profile photo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language: English, Tamil, Hindi, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cart: products, total price, add/remove item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Search query: shared between a search bar and results page.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authentication token: stored after login and used by API calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Theme Context&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Your ThemeProvider is a good real-world example. It reads the saved theme from localStorage, checks the user’s system preference, updates the HTML data-theme attribute, and saves the choice.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;getInitialTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchMedia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;(prefers-color-scheme: dark)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;matches&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;getInitialTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;documentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setAttribute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;data-theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggleTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggleTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How It Works&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;createContext() creates the Context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ThemeProvider holds the actual theme state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;value={{ theme, toggleTheme }} shares both the current theme and the function to change it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;useTheme() lets any component read or update the theme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Using It in a Component
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggleTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggleTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Current theme: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When toggleTheme() changes theme, React automatically re-renders every component that calls useTheme().&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Your Search Context
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your SearchContext is useful when a search input and a results list are in different components.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchContext&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Search Input&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchBar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"text"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;placeholder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Search products..."&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onChange&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setQuery&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchBar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Search Results&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useSearch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SearchResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSearch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;filteredProducts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLowerCase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLowerCase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;filteredProducts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Here, SearchBar updates query, and SearchResults reads the same query — without passing props between them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Wrap Providers in App
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchProvider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./SearchContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Navbar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./Navbar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchBar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./SearchBar&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;SearchResults&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./SearchResults&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Navbar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchBar&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchResults&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;SearchProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeProvider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Any component inside these providers can use useTheme() or useSearch().&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits of useContext&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Benefit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Meaning&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Avoids prop drilling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No need to pass props through components that do not use them. react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Global/shared state&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Theme, user, language, and cart data can be accessed anywhere under the Provider. w3schools&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clean components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Child components become simpler because they do not receive unnecessary props.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Built into React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No external library is required for small and medium apps. react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Automatic updates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;When context value changes, consumers re-render with fresh data. react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Disadvantages of useContext
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Disadvantage&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Why It Matters&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unnecessary re-renders&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;When the Provider value changes, every component using that Context re-renders — even if it uses only one small part of the value. react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Not a full state manager&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Context shares values, but it does not provide selectors, caching, middleware, or advanced state tools like Redux or Zustand. tech-interview&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Harder to test&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Components depend on a Provider, so tests may need to wrap components with that Provider.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Can become messy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Putting too much data in one Context creates a “mega context” that is difficult to maintain. frontend+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Not ideal for frequent updates&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Fast-changing values such as mouse position, scroll position, or typing text can cause many re-renders. frontend&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Important Performance Tip
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This line creates a new object on every render:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, toggleTheme }}&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Because the object reference changes, all context consumers may re-render more often than needed. You can memoize it:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;toggleTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Provider&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;useMemo keeps the same object reference unless theme actually changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Best Practices
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create separate contexts for unrelated data: ThemeContext, AuthContext, CartContext.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not put everything into one huge global context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Context for low-frequency global data such as theme, user, and language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For high-frequency updates, keep state close to the component that needs it or use refs/external stores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expose a custom hook like useTheme() or useSearch() instead of calling useContext directly everywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For larger apps with complex shared state, consider Redux Toolkit, Zustand, or Jotai.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simple Rule&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use useContext when many components — especially deeply nested ones — need the same data. Use normal useState when the data is needed only inside one component or a small part of the UI.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;useEffect is a React Hook used for side effects&lt;/strong&gt; — things like API calls, timers, event listeners, and updating the document title. Its second argument, the dependency array, controls when the effect runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Run Only Once
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Component Mounted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Dependency array: &lt;a href="https://dev.toempty%20array"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why? An empty array tells React that the effect does not depend on any state or prop, so it runs only after the component first appears on screen.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Run on Every Render
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Rendered&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No dependency array is provided.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React runs this effect after every render — on first mount and after every state or prop change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


3. Run When State Changes
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Count changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependency array: [count].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The effect runs on mount and again whenever count changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you use [] instead, "Count changed" prints only once on mount — not when count updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Two States, One Effect
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;count or name changed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dependency array: [count, name].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The effect runs when either count or name changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If only [count] is added, changing name will not run this effect. Also, never omit a value used inside the effect — it can cause stale-value bugs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derived Logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;{count % 2 === 0 ? "Even Number" : "Odd Number"}&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put this logic inside render, not inside useEffect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why? It is directly calculated from existing state. React can re-render and show the correct value automatically. useEffect is for side effects outside React’s normal rendering flow, such as API calls or DOM listeners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. API Call on Mount
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setUsers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We use [] because users should be fetched only once when the component loads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you remove [], the API call runs after every render, causing unnecessary network requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infinite Loop Trap
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This creates an infinite loop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why? The effect runs → count changes → React re-renders → dependency count changed → effect runs again → count changes again. This repeats forever&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fix the Infinite Loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to increment only once:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;prev&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use an empty dependency array [].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the functional update setCount((prev) =&amp;gt; prev + 1) so you always update from the latest state value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not put count in the dependency array if the effect itself changes count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


9. Document Title Sync
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put count inside the dependency array.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Why? The effect uses count, and the title should update every time count changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


10. Cleanup Basic
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Every render adds another click listener. Old listeners are never removed, which can cause memory leaks and repeated function calls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correct Way&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Window clicked&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The returned function is the cleanup function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cleanup runs before the next effect execution and when the component unmounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quick Dependency Table&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Dependency array&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;When effect runs&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;No array&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;After every render react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;[]&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Once after first render / mount react+1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;[count]&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;On mount and when count changes react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;[count, name]&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;On mount and when either changes react&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simple Rule to Remember&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need something once when page loads? Use [].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need something whenever a value changes? Add that value: [value].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Need something after every render? Omit the array.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added a listener, timer, or subscription? Always return a cleanup function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Say goodbye to hook boilerplate, setter functions, and manual state synchronization. Here is how Streamix—powered by a custom compiler and language plugin—is redefining reactivity in React components.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;State management in React has always walked a fine line. Between custom hooks, heavy context providers, &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; tuple destructuring, and explicit &lt;code&gt;.set()&lt;/code&gt; calls, building truly reactive applications can feel like writing boilerplate glue code just to update a primitive value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Enter &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;@epikodelabs/streamix&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;. By combining a robust reactive core with a dedicated compile-time transform and editor plugin, Streamix lets you write &lt;strong&gt;direct variable re-assignment right inside your UI&lt;/strong&gt; without a single hook in sight.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


What are Atoms? (The Reactive Core)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As highlighted in the official documentation section &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/epikodelabs/streamix" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Atoms – Reactive State Primitives&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, atoms are the fundamental building blocks of state in Streamix.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;atom&lt;/strong&gt; represents a discrete unit of reactive state. Unlike traditional state containers that require complex getter/setter wrappers, Streamix atoms act as self-contained primitives that can be read and mutated directly.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Getting Started: Configuration
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To unlock direct reactive assignment and ensure your editor handles the syntax smoothly, you only need two quick configuration pieces.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


1. Configure the Vite Plugin (&lt;code&gt;vite.config.mjs&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Add the Streamix React Vite plugin (&lt;code&gt;sx&lt;/code&gt;) to your build pipeline:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;defineConfig&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;vite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@vitejs/plugin-react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;sx&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@epikodelabs/streamix/react/vite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;defineConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;plugins&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


2. Configure the TypeScript Server Plugin (&lt;code&gt;tsconfig.json&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To ensure your editor (like VS Code) understands the compile-time transforms and provides proper autocompletion without type complaints, register the TSServer plugin in your &lt;code&gt;tsconfig.json&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"compilerOptions"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"plugins"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@epikodelabs/streamix/react/editor/tsserver"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;

&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


Truly Pure Reactive Syntax in Action
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once configured, check out how clean and readable your component code becomes:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;atom&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@epikodelabs/streamix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Define a reactive primitive using an atom&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;atom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Hello, Streamix!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;HeaderComponent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* 
Referencing the atom directly inside JSX automatically 
subscribes the component to reactive updates.
*/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Direct re-assignment! Handled seamlessly by the compiler. */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;React + Streamix is Live!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Update Title
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Notice what is missing? &lt;strong&gt;No &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; hooks, no &lt;code&gt;setState()&lt;/code&gt;, no &lt;code&gt;atom.set()&lt;/code&gt;, and no manual subscription wiring.&lt;/strong&gt; You simply write intuitive JavaScript assignments, and the compiler handles the heavy lifting under the hood.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Why This Integration is a Game Changer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Direct Assignment (&lt;code&gt;=&lt;/code&gt;) DX:&lt;/strong&gt; Update state naturally as if it were a simple variable while preserving full reactive re-rendering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zero Hook Boilerplate:&lt;/strong&gt; Forget calling subscription hooks or managing dependency arrays inside your components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No Tuple Destructuring:&lt;/strong&gt; Say goodbye to managing &lt;code&gt;[state, setState]&lt;/code&gt; pairs across your codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;First-Class Editor Support:&lt;/strong&gt; The TSServer plugin ensures your TypeScript environment stays happy and fully typed out-of-the-box.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Async-Ready Core:&lt;/strong&gt; Built on robust reactive primitives and async iterators to handle event streams effortlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Give It a Spin
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to experiment with compiler-driven reactivity in your next React SPA or Vite project, check out the official repository:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Repository:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/epikodelabs/streamix" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;github.com/epikodelabs/streamix&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Discussions:&lt;/strong&gt; Jump into the GitHub discussions to share feedback, feature requests, and early impressions!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What are your thoughts on shifting state management logic to a compile-time transform with direct assignment? Drop a comment below and let's discuss! 👇&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Happy coding!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Stop reaching for a global store too early. Identify which of the &lt;strong&gt;five kinds of state&lt;/strong&gt; you have and pick the narrowest tool that works, and never manage server state as if it were client state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Contents
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You wired up a global store for a toggle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick the narrowest scope that works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The five kinds of state, by scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A cheat sheet: state type to tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Local state vs a server-cache hook in code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server state is not client state&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Common mistakes that cost hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takeaways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where to go next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


You wired up a global store for a toggle
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A teammate opens the codebase and finds a Redux store, three slices, a middleware, and a set of action creators. They follow the wiring to see what important, app-wide thing it manages. The answer: whether a dropdown menu is open. One boolean. It lives in a global store, reachable from every component in the app, persisted across routes, traced through DevTools, to remember if a little arrow points up or down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the most common failure in frontend, and it is not a beginner mistake, senior teams do it constantly. State management has a reputation for being hard, so people reach for the heaviest tool they know &lt;strong&gt;first&lt;/strong&gt;, before they have a problem that needs it. The result is apps where a one-line change touches four files, and where nobody can tell which state actually matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The skill is not learning Redux, Zustand, or Jotai. The skill is knowing &lt;strong&gt;what kind of state you have&lt;/strong&gt; and putting it in the smallest place that works. Most state does not belong in a global store. A lot of it is not even client state at all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📌 &lt;strong&gt;Who this is for:&lt;/strong&gt; Frontend developers, comfortable with &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/javascript-for-the-browser" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;JavaScript&lt;/a&gt; and React components, who keep hearing "just use a state library" and want a framework for deciding &lt;strong&gt;where&lt;/strong&gt; each piece of state should live, not which library to install. No prior Redux or Zustand experience assumed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Pick the narrowest scope that works
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;State should live in the narrowest scope that still works, and move outward only when something outside that scope genuinely needs it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The one rule this whole article is about&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Almost every state decision is a question of &lt;strong&gt;scope&lt;/strong&gt;: who needs to read this value, and who needs to change it? If only one component cares, it is local. If two siblings care, lift it to their parent. If the whole app cares, it might be global. The mistake is starting at the widest scope "just in case", you pay the complexity cost forever for a need that usually never arrives.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the real world&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In tech&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A reminder only you need, on a sticky note on your own desk&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Local UI state, useState inside one component&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A note your deskmate also needs, stuck where you both sit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lifted state, held in the shared parent of two components&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A policy the whole company must see, on the lobby noticeboard&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Global state, a store every component can read&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Putting your lunch order on the company noticeboard&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A toggle in a global Redux store, wrong desk entirely&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Where you write a note depends on who needs to read it.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep the sticky note on the right desk. Most of what gets pinned to the global noticeboard is a private reminder that only one component ever reads, it just got promoted out of habit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The five kinds of state, by scope
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before you can choose a tool, you have to name what you are holding. Almost everything falls into one of five buckets, ordered from narrowest scope to widest. The further right you go, the more tools and ceremony you take on, so the goal is always to stay as far left as the requirement allows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-fCJldmVyeW9uZSBuZWVkcyBpdCJ8IG5fZ2xvYmFsCiAgbl9nbG9iYWwgLS4tPnwiaXQgbGl2ZXMgb24gYSBzZXJ2ZXIifCBuX3NlcnZlcgogIG5fc2VydmVyIC0uLT58Iml0IGJlbG9uZ3MgaW4gdGhlIGxpbmsifCBuX3VybAogIG5fbG9jYWwgLS4tPiBuX2NvbXAKICBuX2xpZnRlZCAtLi0-IG5fcGFyZW50CiAgbl9nbG9iYWwgLS4tPiBuX3N0b3JlCiAgbl9zZXJ2ZXIgLS4tPiBuX3F1ZXJ5CiAgbl91cmwgLS4tPiBuX3JvdXRlcg%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-fCJldmVyeW9uZSBuZWVkcyBpdCJ8IG5fZ2xvYmFsCiAgbl9nbG9iYWwgLS4tPnwiaXQgbGl2ZXMgb24gYSBzZXJ2ZXIifCBuX3NlcnZlcgogIG5fc2VydmVyIC0uLT58Iml0IGJlbG9uZ3MgaW4gdGhlIGxpbmsifCBuX3VybAogIG5fbG9jYWwgLS4tPiBuX2NvbXAKICBuX2xpZnRlZCAtLi0-IG5fcGFyZW50CiAgbl9nbG9iYWwgLS4tPiBuX3N0b3JlCiAgbl9zZXJ2ZXIgLS4tPiBuX3F1ZXJ5CiAgbl91cmwgLS4tPiBuX3JvdXRlcg%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" alt="State types by scope, start at the left, move right only when forced." width="1583" height="436"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;State types by scope, start at the left, move right only when forced.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Does only one component use it?&lt;/strong&gt;: Keep it local with useState. A form input, a hover flag, an open/closed toggle, these almost never leave the component that owns them. This is where most state should stay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Do a couple of nearby components need it?&lt;/strong&gt;: Lift it to their closest common parent and pass it down as props. Two siblings sharing a selected tab? The tab index lives in the parent. No library required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Does genuinely everything need it, far apart in the tree?&lt;/strong&gt;: Now consider Context or a small global store, for things like the signed-in user, theme, or feature flags. The bar is high: it must be needed in many distant places and rarely change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Does the data actually live on a server?&lt;/strong&gt;: Stop. This is not client state. Use a server-state library (TanStack Query, SWR, RTK Query) that handles fetching, caching, and refetching. Do not copy it into a store.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Should the value survive a refresh or be shareable via link?&lt;/strong&gt;: Put it in the URL. A search query, active filter, page number, or selected tab often belongs in search params so a copied link reproduces the exact view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A cheat sheet: state type to tool
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Map each kind of state to its example and the simplest tool that fits. If you can answer "what kind of state is this?" you have already answered "what should I reach for?". Notice how few rows actually call for a global store.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;State type&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;The right tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Local UI&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Input value, dropdown open, hover, an accordion's expanded panel&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;useReducer&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lifted / shared&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Selected row two sibling panels both read&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;State in the common parent + props&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Global app&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Signed-in user, theme, feature flags&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Context, or a small store (Zustand)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server-cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Product list, user profile, anything from an API&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;TanStack Query / SWR / RTK Query&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;URL&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Search term, filters, page number, active tab&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Router search params (&lt;code&gt;useSearchParams&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pick the row first, the tool second.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;strong&gt;Tip:&lt;/strong&gt; When in doubt, default to &lt;strong&gt;local&lt;/strong&gt;. It is trivial to lift state upward later when a second component needs it. Pulling a tangle of global state back down once everything depends on it is a refactor nobody volunteers for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Local state vs a server-cache hook in code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is the contrast that matters most in practice. The first block is &lt;strong&gt;local state&lt;/strong&gt;, a value owned and changed entirely on the client. The second is &lt;strong&gt;server state&lt;/strong&gt;, data that lives in a database and is only borrowed by the browser. They look superficially similar but have completely different needs, so they get completely different tools.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Counter.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Local UI state: the client owns it outright.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// No network, no cache, no "is it stale?", just a value and a setter.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Clicked &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; times
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useUser.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Server-cache state: the SERVER owns the truth.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// The library handles caching, loading, errors, and refetching.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useQuery&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@tanstack/react-query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;;

async function fetchUser(id: string) {
const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`);
if (!res.ok) throw new Error(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Failed to load user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;);
return res.json() as Promise&amp;lt;{ id: string; name: string }&amp;gt;;
}

export function useUser(id: string) {
// We don't store the user in useState or a global store.
// We describe HOW to fetch it; the cache is managed for us.
return useQuery({
queryKey: [&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;\"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;, id],
queryFn: () =&amp;gt; fetchUser(id),
staleTime: 60_000, // treat as fresh for 60s before refetching
});
}

// In a component:
//   const { data, isLoading, error } = useUser(userId);
// You get loading + error + cached data for free, no useEffect soup,
// no manual setState, no duplicating the response into a store.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The counter needs nothing but &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;. The user needs caching, a loading flag, an error path, and a strategy for staleness, all of which the query library provides. Trying to manage the user with &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; recreates a worse version of that library by hand; putting the counter in a global store adds machinery a button never asked for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Server state is not client state
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the single most clarifying idea in modern frontend, so it gets its own section. &lt;strong&gt;Client state&lt;/strong&gt; is state your app invents and owns: a toggle, a form draft, the current theme. You are the source of truth. &lt;strong&gt;Server state&lt;/strong&gt; is a copy of data that lives somewhere else, a database behind an API. You do not own it; you are borrowing a snapshot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That difference changes everything. Server state can go &lt;strong&gt;stale&lt;/strong&gt; the moment you fetch it, because someone else might change the record. It needs caching so you do not refetch on every render, refetching so it stays current, and shared loading and error states. None of those concerns exist for client state. This is why purpose-built server-state libraries exist, and why shoving API responses into a general-purpose store is a mismatch: a store has no concept of staleness, background refetch, or request deduplication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ &lt;strong&gt;The tell-tale sign:&lt;/strong&gt; If you find yourself writing &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; to fetch data and then &lt;code&gt;setState&lt;/code&gt; to store it, and then more code to track loading and errors, you are hand-rolling a server-state library. Use a real one. It will be less code and far more correct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once you split these two, your "global store" usually shrinks to almost nothing. Most of what people pile into Redux is server state that belongs in a query cache. Take that out, and what is left, the genuinely global, client-owned stuff, is often small enough for plain Context or a tiny store.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Common mistakes that cost hours
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A global store for everything.&lt;/strong&gt; Reaching for Redux/Zustand on day one, then routing a dropdown toggle and a form input through it. Every trivial change becomes a four-file edit. Default to local; promote outward only when a real second consumer appears.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Duplicating server data in a store.&lt;/strong&gt; Fetching a list, copying it into a global store, and then fighting to keep that copy in sync with the server. Now you have two sources of truth and stale-data bugs. Let a server-state library own the cache; read it where you need it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Prop-drilling instead of composition.&lt;/strong&gt; Threading a prop through five intermediate components that do not use it, then "fixing" it with global state. Often the real fix is &lt;strong&gt;component composition&lt;/strong&gt;, pass JSX as children so the data-owning parent renders the consumer directly. See &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/component-architecture-and-design-systems" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Component Architecture &amp;amp; Design Systems&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Context for high-frequency updates.&lt;/strong&gt; Putting fast-changing values (mouse position, every keystroke) in a single Context re-renders every consumer on every change. Context is for low-frequency, widely-read values like theme or user, not a performance-sensitive firehose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The whole article in seven lines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State decisions are scope decisions: who reads it, who changes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick the narrowest scope that works; move outward only when forced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five kinds: local UI, lifted/shared, global app, server-cache, URL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Default to local &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;; lifting later is cheap, un-globalizing is not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server state is not client state, give it a query library, not a store.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Never duplicate server data into a global store; you create a second truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reach for composition before prop-drilling, and before going global.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where to go next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;State lives inside components, so the cleaner your component boundaries, the more obvious every state decision becomes. Strengthen the layers above and below this one:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solidify the language underneath it all in &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/javascript-for-the-browser" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;JavaScript for the Browser&lt;/a&gt;, closures and references are exactly what hooks rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn how composition replaces prop-drilling in &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/component-architecture-and-design-systems" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Component Architecture &amp;amp; Design Systems&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the full &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/career-paths/frontend-engineer" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Engineer career path&lt;/a&gt; to see where state management sits in the bigger picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The next time you feel the urge to install a state library, pause and ask one question: &lt;strong&gt;what kind of state is this, and what is the narrowest scope that works?&lt;/strong&gt; Most of the time, the answer is &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;, and that is a feature, not a shortcoming.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/state-management-in-frontend-apps" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TheSimplifiedTech&lt;/a&gt;, where this guide is interactive, with in-browser terminal labs and diagrams. Learn cloud and DevOps by doing, no videos.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Polling is the honest trade-off here: a React or Next.js frontend can refresh basic feature flags from a backend API, but it will not receive changes in real time. &lt;strong&gt;Short answer:&lt;/strong&gt; fetch a non-sensitive value through your own backend on load, poll at a measured interval, and record the evaluated state beside each logistics event that may later become incident evidence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Choice&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Browser delivery&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Reconstruction evidence&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Best fit&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Shared REST API&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Poll through your backend&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Add your own release record and event instrumentation&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A stable HTTP boundary across backend providers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;LaunchDarkly&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Dedicated client SDK&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Use its flag and audit tooling&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams that want a specialist flag platform&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Unleash&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Client or proxy patterns&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Use its event and change-history features&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams that value an open-source option&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;ConfigCat&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Client SDK and polling modes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Use its product tooling around configuration changes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams that want a focused hosted flag service&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I would try Infrai for the non-sensitive UI-toggle part of this workflow when one plain REST contract matters more than specialist flag analytics: the application-facing contract can stay put while the provider behind the capability changes. Its public discovery surface exposes request and response schemas, which removes guesswork at the integration boundary. Every documented capability ships runnable examples in 10 languages. Breadth is real: 295 routes across 20 modules under one key, so a small team can keep flag reads and adjacent backend calls behind one credential and one set of conventions. It does not remove the need to own incident evidence.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How should a React frontend poll backend feature flags?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful question is not merely, "Was &lt;code&gt;new-route-panel&lt;/code&gt; enabled?" It is: which value did this user receive when the dispatch action happened, in which region, and under which application release? Imagine a dispatcher in the EU confirms a route at 14:03, support gets a complaint at 14:40, and the flag changed between those times. The current flag value proves nothing about the earlier screen. The dispatch event needs its own evaluated value and release identifier, while a release record explains the intended rollout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Evidence wins.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A flag service answers only part of that chain. For a staged launch across US and EU users, keep targeting inputs on the server, return only the boolean or other non-sensitive value the component needs, and attach the evaluated value to the business event. Do not ship an administration key or a full internal flag document to the browser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep it boring.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These flags have no built-in change audit log or evaluation analytics. They also have no parent-child dependencies, deleted flags have no recycle bin, and clients poll. A release note can preserve who intended a change and why; event instrumentation can preserve what the customer actually saw. You need both if reconstruction is the decision axis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Keep the provider call behind one backend route
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The server route below calls one verified endpoint. It refuses arbitrary flag names, keeps the bearer key server-side, checks upstream errors, and forwards &lt;code&gt;Retry-After&lt;/code&gt; on a rate limit. The response shape is intentionally read through a configured JSON Pointer because the value location should come from the live discovery schema, not a guessed field name.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/api/flags/[key]/route.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NextRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;publicFlags&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;new-route-panel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;readPointer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pointer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;pointer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;pointer&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;split&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;part&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;part&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/~1/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/~0/g&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;~&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;part&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Record&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;part&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

