&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NextResponse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Look up the capability through public discovery before setting &lt;code&gt;INFRAI_FLAG_VALUE_POINTER&lt;/code&gt;; the schema is the contract. That extra environment setting may look like config. I dislike config bloat too. Here it is cheaper than silently coupling production code to an invented response property.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Poll slowly, fail closed, and measure the boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The component fetches immediately, then every 30 seconds. That means a toggle can remain stale for roughly one interval plus request latency. Pick the interval from an explicit propagation budget, then benchmark request volume and user-visible delay. Ten thousand open tabs at a five-second interval would create about 2,000 requests per second before retries. Arithmetic first.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

